---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../content/landing";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service — PostStack"
  description="Terms for using PostStack: accounts, user content, connected platforms, service availability, responsibilities and contact."
>
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: 2026-10-27</p>

  <h2>1. Acceptance and service</h2>
  <p>
    These terms describe use of PostStack, a social media management product for publishing and
    scheduling content, managing conversations, automating replies and organising contacts.
    By using the service you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, stop using it.
    PostStack is provided by Paweł Jurczyk (TechSkills Academy), Poland. For a hosted installation
    operated by someone else, that operator's service agreement also applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may run the source-available software on your own infrastructure or use a hosted
    installation where offered. Self-hosted operators manage their infrastructure, backups,
    credentials and compliance. Use and redistribution of the software remain subject to its
    Elastic License 2.0 and any separately agreed commercial licence; these terms do not grant
    additional software or hosting rights.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Accounts and permitted use</h2>
  <p>
    Provide accurate account details, protect your login and API credentials, and connect only
    accounts you own or are authorised to manage. You are responsible for activity you authorise
    in your workspace. If you act for an organisation, you must have authority to do so.
    Notify your instance operator promptly if you suspect unauthorised access.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not use PostStack for unlawful content, spam, misleading activity, infringement of others'
    rights or access to accounts without permission. Do not interfere with the service or misuse
    connected platforms. An operator may restrict access where needed to address these activities;
    you may stop using the service and request data deletion as described in our Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Your content</h2>
  <p>
    You retain ownership of your content. You grant the instance operator only the permission
    needed to store, process and transmit your content to provide the features you request.
    You must hold the rights and permissions needed for your videos, images, captions, music
    and other material, including any required advertising and AI-content disclosures.
    Review your selected account, content and publishing settings before sending or scheduling.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Platform integrations</h2>
  <p>
    Connecting an account authorises PostStack to perform the supported actions you request
    within the permissions you grant. You must comply with each platform's applicable terms,
    community guidelines and API policies, including{" "}
    <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/terms-of-service">TikTok's Terms of Service</a>,{" "}
    <a href="https://www.facebook.com/terms.php">Meta's Terms</a> and{" "}
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube's Terms of Service</a> for Google/YouTube
    integrations. TikTok publishing also requires compliance with its music and branded-content
    rules where applicable. PostStack is independent of these platforms and does not imply
    their endorsement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Available actions depend on your account permissions, API access and the platform's review
    requirements. For TikTok, an upload may be delivered as a draft requiring completion in the
    TikTok app; Direct Post availability depends on the connected application's approval and
    configuration. API limits, processing delays and policy changes can affect delivery.
    Scheduling does not guarantee publication at an exact time or successful publication.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data and privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> describes connected-account data, website cookies,
    telemetry and deletion. Disconnecting an integration stops future use of that connection;
    it does not automatically remove content already published on another platform. For hosted
    application data requests, contact your instance operator. Self-hosted operators control
    their stored data and retention.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Availability and responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by applicable law and any service agreement, PostStack is provided
    “as is” and “as available”. We do not guarantee uninterrupted operation, error-free delivery
    or continued access to a third-party API. Keep copies of important content and check
    publishing results. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or
    consequential losses arising from service interruptions, failed publication or platform
    account restrictions. Nothing in these terms excludes liability or consumer rights that
    cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the product changes. Material changes will be identified by
    the updated date and communicated through the website or the applicable hosted service.
    Questions, complaints and requests can be sent to{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="legal-back"><a href="/">← Back to PostStack</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
